xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:14:One **scoop-claim**, not a THREAT: Schenk, Zenodo 18622130 (2026-02-12), file unchanged this session (PDF SHA-256 `6ba4088386eb40affbb4abad54bb8e1574de09d00da9d1fbeac9f5c88d160f24`, 569113 bytes). If sound it would *imply* the promoted N\(\le 5\) closures and the cusp/homology theorems, not contradict them. Registered 2026-09-01; still unaudited. No v2.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:16:Highest-value **campaign miss** (older than 60 days, absent from campaign greps of `2512.07986` / `2503.07099` / `Kulikov`): Orevkov arXiv:2512.07986, addendum to Kulikov 2503.07099, classifies germs \((\mathbb{C}^2,0)\to(\mathbb{C}^2,0)\) ramified along an irreducible branch whose image is \(u^{d_1}=v^{d_2}\). Jacobian is a power of a cusp, **not** a Keller identity. **STRUCTURE** for the one-cusp / A2 local model and for `OPEN[A2-U-BOUND]`; not a close.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:20:**Promoted items this sweep must not be scooped or contradicted.** N=4-CHECKED-CLOSED and N=5 SOUND-BY-DEPENDENCY-AUDIT; THEOREMs NO-PUSHFORWARD, CENTRAL-RANK, CUSP-PARITY, ORBIFOLD-CAGE, CUSP-A-EMPTY; realized-curve kills of \((9,6,2)\) and \((9,6,4)\).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:22:**Named OPENs used as bearing targets.** `OPEN[A2-U-BOUND]`, `OPEN[HOMCOVER-CUSP-A-N8]`, `OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-U]`, `OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-COMPLETION-UNDECLARED]`, `OPEN[COMPANION-R0-REALISATION]`, `OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]`, `OPEN[CARD-C-SOURCE-NORMAL-FORM]`, the one-cusp horn (B3), case-(A) survivors at \(N\ge 8\), N\(\ge 6\) census / SIROCCO–ZvK pipeline, MODULAR-vs-PROVEN.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:30:**F1. Schenk, *A valuation-theoretic proof of the Jacobian conjecture in dimension two*, Zenodo 18622130, 2026-02-12.** Unchanged: created 2026-02-12, updated 2026-02-13, one file `Jacobi in N=2.pdf`. SHA-256 this session `6ba4088386eb40affbb4abad54bb8e1574de09d00da9d1fbeac9f5c88d160f24`. Scoop-claim of JC2 over algebraically closed char 0 via Stein factorization, affine-dicritical Rees degeneration, positivity of the Jacobian two-form, triviality of finite étale covers of \(\mathbb{A}^2\), Zariski’s Main Theorem. **Scoop-claim of the whole plane problem, not a THREAT** to N\(\le 5\), the cusp theorems, or the two curve kills. Not audited here.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:44:**F8. Window recap already hashed 2026-09-01 (no new versions this session).** Kistner–Shaska 2608.02863 (graded dim-3; Prop. 3.21: no cyclic-cone descent to a two-variable Keller pair); Gao 2608.00222 (\(n\ge 3\)); Mondello 2608.02634 (char-2 plane); Shaska 2607.20210v2 (every graded plane Keller map is an automorphism); Jelonek 2607.20597; van Dobben de Bruyn 2608.27341; Pissolato 2608.19069; Migus 2607.21572v3 (real Keller maps with non-dense image; \(S_2\subseteq\{2m:m\ge 3\}\) and JC2 \(\Rightarrow S_2=\emptyset\)). SuperMind HEAD `8b376296` (2026-08-05) unchanged. Strinz `(75,125)` HEAD `16ae8b263cb8` (2026-08-30) unchanged. Helali Zenodo 21479814 v1.0.1 (2026-07-21) unchanged. Kakarottoooo public-preprint-v1 (2026-08-10) unchanged. Roy van Rijn HEAD `43028937` (2026-09-02) is lattice-foundry / Elkies rank-17 / Q80 work, not a plane Keller claim.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:56:Target: post-2020 dicriticals of polynomial maps \(\mathbb{A}^2\to\mathbb{A}^2\), Jelonek non-properness sets, Domrina–Orevkov-style low-degree classifications. Bearing on `OPEN[RESIDUAL-TO-DOMRINA-STATE]` and the one-cusp horn (local dicritical picture at infinity).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:58:**F11. Corral–Gómez-Martínez–Senovilla-Sanz, *Cuspidal dicritical foliations and analytical invariants of cusps*, arXiv:2605.30634v1, 2026-05-28.** SHA-256 `d3bc4da7093756084cada50f9eb0a90344d9108aae488454fcb42b999e176cd1`. Local germs of foliations on \((\mathbb{C}^2,0)\): a foliation is *cuspidal dicritical* if after the minimal resolution of a cusp it is totally \(E\)-dicritical along the cuspidal divisor. The invariant curves through free points of \(E\) are equisingular cusps, not in general analytically equivalent. Main theorems: \(\ell\)-transversality with a minimal standard basis of 1-forms freezes the first \(\ell+2\) generators of the semimodule \(\Lambda_C\) of differential values; a bound on the divisorial value \(\nu_E(\omega_{\mathcal{F}})\) in terms of the conductor of \(\Lambda_C\) forces \(\Lambda\)-constancy of the whole family. Explicit conductor formula \(c(\Lambda_C)=\tilde u_{s+1}-n-m+1\). **STRUCTURE** for the local analytic classification of one-Puiseux-pair branches and for the vocabulary “dicritical along a cusp.” **IRRELEVANT** as a close of Domrina–Orevkov or of a global polynomial Keller map: these are local foliations, not polynomial self-maps of \(\mathbb{A}^2\), and the Jacobian of a Keller map is a *constant*, not a foliation 1-form.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:68:## 3. Fundamental groups, \(S_n\)-covers, HOM-COVER, Tokunaga school
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:70:Target: \(\pi_1\) of complements of rational cuspidal plane curves; \(S_n\)-covers branched at singular curves; homology of branched covers (HOM-COVER razor); Tokunaga-school updates. Bearing on `OPEN[SOURCE-OPEN-U]`, `OPEN[HOMCOVER-CUSP-A-N8]`, THEOREM NO-PUSHFORWARD / CENTRAL-RANK.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:72:**F14. Orevkov, *On germs of mappings \(\mathbb{C}^2\to\mathbb{C}^2\)*, arXiv:2512.07986v1, 2025-12-08.** SHA-256 `a25645002759138455b64db053c00771f4cf203d6ec386d2c33969ecffe94065` (31 pp.). **Campaign miss** (grep of `2512.07986` empty). Addendum to Kulikov 2503.07099 (F15). Classifies analytic germs \(F:(\mathbb{C}^2,0)\to(\mathbb{C}^2,0)\) that are finite covers of degree \(N\), branched over \(C=\{u^{d_1}=v^{d_2}\}\) with \(\gcd(d_1,d_2)=1\) and \(\min(d_1,d_2)>1\), under (A1)–(A2): \(F\) analytic, \(F(0)=0\), and \(F\) bijective on each component of \(F^{-1}(C)\). Ramification order \(n\) along the singular locus \(\widetilde C\) means \(\mathrm{div}(JF)=(n-1)\widetilde C\). Completeness: every such germ is, after swapping \(d_1\leftrightarrow d_2\), one of two Belyi/Davenport–Zannier families (a)/(b), built from a Belyi function with ramification type \((\alpha;(n,1^{N-1});\beta)\). Explicit formulae for \(n=2\) (quadratic ramification) and half of \(n=3\). Uses Orevkov 2001 “JC at infinity” toric-cover machinery (his [8], with a recorded misprint in §1.2). Jacobian identity is \(J(F)=\mu(y^{k_2}-x^{k_1})^{n-1}\), **not a constant**. **STRUCTURE** for the local ramified model of a one-cusp (torus-knot) branch, for HOM-COVER’s local covering data, and for Chisini-type uniqueness of surfaces from ramification images. **IRRELEVANT as a threat** to NO-PUSHFORWARD / CENTRAL-RANK (those are global homology of \(S_n\)-covers of affine complements). Does **not** produce an \(S_4\) cover of a realized \((9,6,*)\) curve.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:74:**F15. Kulikov, *On irreducible germs of generic morphisms*, arXiv:2503.07099v1, 2025-03-10.** SHA-256 `a78700a47e1ffafa71d9fb2b232a3250c3442c17b715de96e958942c1043245d` (39 pp.). **Campaign miss.** Irreducible germs of finite generic morphisms \(S\to\mathbb{P}^2\) whose branch-curve germs are equisingular to \(x^{k_1}-y^{k_2}=0\). Parent of F14; extends Chisini-type uniqueness. **STRUCTURE** same as F14; not an \(S_n\)-existence criterion for polynomial one-place curves.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:76:**F16. Guerville-Ballé, *LA-MOKA: a combinatorial discretization algorithm for the braid monodromy of line arrangements*, arXiv:2607.29333v1, 2026-07-31.** SHA-256 `0ce109833f8e9b69727c606fe26588eea4d02149df730e319f852e976860cb97`. Certified braid monodromy for *complex line arrangements* by \(k\)-grid discretization with explicit non-crossing conditions (C1)/(C2); Sage implementation `guerville-balle/LA-MOKA`, HEAD `30948b06` (2026-07-29). Benchmark vs SIROCCO on \(n=5..9\) lines: SIROCCO max \(\sim 500\)s at \(n=9\), LA-MOKA \(<0.6\)s. Cites Sage 10.9 (2026) and SIROCCO. **STRUCTURE** for the SIROCCO/ZvK ecosystem (F24). **Does not apply** to the realized \((9,6,2)\)/\((9,6,4)\) curves (not line arrangements). No threat to the two curve kills.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:78:**F17. Artal Bartolo, *Topology of complex plane curves: braid monodromy, local and global problems*, arXiv:2604.26596v1, 2026-04-29.** SHA-256 `6eb671d611868d13d2e3aa8f52893ecce29b7e5528e7a94846e47ce23abd5712`. Historical/survey notes on local and global embeddings of plane projective curves via braid monodromy. **STRUCTURE** as a desk reference; no new existence/nonexistence theorem for \(S_n\)-covers of one-place rational curves.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:88:## 4. Degree-termination, Mason–Stothers / abc-with-derivatives, unit Wronskians, one-cusp (A2)
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:90:Target: degree-termination for polynomial ODE / Wronskian systems; Mason–Stothers and abc-for-polynomials with derivatives; unit Wronskians \(qr'-p's=\mathrm{const}\); one-cusp (\(A_2\)) singularities at infinity of Keller maps. Bearing: **`OPEN[A2-U-BOUND]`** (bound \(U\) equivalently \(\deg q,\deg r,\deg s\) in terms of \(e\) on the E1-wall).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:98:**F22. Grabowski, *On algebraic integrability of vector fields with rational function coefficients that separate variables*, arXiv:2609.00974v1, 2026-09-02.** SHA-256 `442cc9a3374878e301bbd3a219a383472cb23dad89b5623a39493bf929a6b7ab`. Necessary and sufficient condition for a variable-separating rational vector field to have a maximal-dimensional ring of rational first integrals, via reduction modulo almost all primes (Grothendieck–Katz \(p\)-curvature for this class), plus explicit formulae for the integrable coefficients. **STRUCTURE** for polynomial/rational ODE degree-termination in the *separable* class; the A2 3\(\times\)3 Wronskian system on the E1-wall is not a separated-variables vector field. **IRRELEVANT** as a close of `OPEN[A2-U-BOUND]`.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:100:**F14 revisited.** Orevkov’s germs have \(J(F)=\mu(y^{k_2}-x^{k_1})^{n-1}\). For \(n=2\) this is a simple-cusp Jacobian divisor, the local model of an \(A_2\) (or more generally \(A_{2m}\)) ramification. Completeness of the germ classification does **not** bound the *global* polynomial degrees \(U\) of a Keller map whose compactification has one cusp at infinity: those germs are not Keller. **STRUCTURE** for the local normal form the horn already uses; no U-bound.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:110:**F23. Almirón–Olivares-Fernández, *Topological representations of free numerical semigroups via iterated torus knots*, arXiv:2412.01613v2, 2025-10-06 (to appear, Res. Math. Sci.).** SHA-256 `d65a2f34d2d4a874ea6191841074d668499ea87cfe52e6b2286375b920b0e5a6`. Associates a family of iterated torus knots in \(S^3\) to a free numerical semigroup; computes \(\pi_1\) of each complement; all knots in the family have the same Alexander polynomial, equal (up to a factor) to the Poincaré series of the semigroup. Consequence: families of iterated torus knots with the Alexander polynomial of an irreducible plane-curve singularity that are **not isotopic** to the associated algebraic knot. **STRUCTURE** for the horn’s “torus-knot-with-relators” group family (CENTRAL-RANK / CUSP-PARITY consume this topology): Alexander polynomials do not separate algebraic from non-algebraic iterated-torus knots of a given free semigroup. **Does not** realize or forbid a polynomial one-place curve of a prescribed \(\delta\)-sequence.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:126:BLZ 2104.13709v2 (AGT 2024) remains the licensed source of Thm 6.4; hash `ac64acd8…` from 2026-09-01. Zemke 2025–2026 papers still do not return to plane algebraic curves. **No equality-case successor.**
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:134:**F27. SIROCCO2 upstream.** GitHub `miguelmarco/SIROCCO2`, latest release **2.1.1**, commit `2195fccda542` (2025-08-11, pkg-config). No 2026 commit. Sage optional SPKG remains 2.1.1. Practical status unchanged: Interval-Newton certified tubes.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:152:**F30. Kudo–Yokoyama, *Degree bounds and synchronization in Gröbner basis computations for affine semi-regular systems*, arXiv:2404.03530v4, replacement 2026-09-02.** SHA-256 `2d1bcb23554e4418f7ef298d1723b4ca75dba16fa835a63ce2de9c891d2c8ec5`. Solving-degree bounds for affine (not necessarily homogeneous) semi-regular sequences via homogenization and the first degree-fall; synchronization of Buchberger-like computations among an affine system, its homogenization, and its highest-degree homogeneous parts. Cryptographic semi-regularity guarantees correspondence until the degree of regularity. **STRUCTURE** for complexity of the A2-cell Groebner jobs and for encoding-faithfulness preflights; **does not** certify any campaign EMPTY.
