## 3. Task (2)(a) — the δ_1' = 0 question (source)

`SOURCE-READ` p.179 Def 5.1(3): the printed formula gives raw
`δ_1' = 1 − 35·29/(5·203) = 0` for `(21,14;15;6)`, before the `(k+1)`
factor; Def 5.1 only needs the strict tower `D_2 ⊋ D_1`, i.e. `δ_1' > δ_2'`,
satisfied. p.187: `0 < δ_1 < 1`, `A > 1` are consequences of `k = 0`
(`U_2 < V_2`), not hypotheses of Def 5.1; here `A' = 1`, the p.188 Galois
step is vacuous (prop55k `OPEN[A-PRIME-ONE]`), and `b12 = b13 = true` in the
batch invariants is this vacuity, not a licence. p.190: with `δ_2 = −1` the
general point is `σ_1 = at^{−1} + b + πt^{δ_1}` and `y → y − ax − b`
normalises it; at `δ_1' = 0` the `b` merges with `π`, so the disc `D_1` is
"integral": its 18 `g`-roots and 12 `f`-roots are `y = a_j + o(1)` with
distinct constants (Prop A.5 simplicity, unchanged for `J = cγ^k`). Hence
`deg_x g = 3`, `deg_x f = 2`, `deg_x h = 1`, and the leading
`x`-coefficients are `ḡ_σ = g_3`, `T_σ = f_2`, coprime with simple roots.
The batch chart forces `(g_3, f_2) = (−h_1^3, h_1^2)`, sharing the factor
